course: dictionary
lesson: 15541
title: Sunsetting: a gentle word for ending
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Sunsetting» is a word that sounds soft and pretty, like a sunset, but in business it means ending something. «The company is sunsetting its old music app next year.» The clue is the app: an app cannot be sunset like the sky, so the sentence is about stopping it.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Closing down or ending both fit. Swap one into the sentence and check that it still makes sense. «The company is closing down its old music app next year» does, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Companies use this word to make bad news sound gentler. «The bus company is sunsetting route 7 in June» sounds calmer than «The bus company is stopping route 7 for good.» Both say the same thing, so when you read jargon, look past the soft wording to the real meaning.
fact: «Sunsetting» (as a verb) means ending a product, service or law, often slowly.
fact: Sunsetting is business jargon, and it is a euphemism: a softer way of saying something harsh.
fact: «The company is sunsetting its old app» means the app will be shut down.
fact: «Sunset» as a noun means the time when the sun goes down.
fact: A good check is to swap in closing down or ending: if the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
exercise: «The company is sunsetting its old email service next month.» What does sunsetting mean here? | Singing a new song about it | *Ending the service | Teaching people to use it | Making it bigger and better
exercise: «The sunset turned the sky pink and gold.» What does sunset mean here? | A kind of pink paint | The end of a school day | *The time when the sun goes down | The start of the morning
exercise: Why do companies often say sunsetting instead of closing down? | *To make shutting something down sound gentler | Because it is the name of a famous song | Because the word is shorter and faster to type | Because it means the product is brand new
test: «The council is sunsetting the old bus route in June.» What does this most likely mean? | *The bus route is being ended | The bus route is being built on a hill | The bus route is starting for the first time | The bus route is being painted yellow
test: «We walked home after the sunset.» Which word means the time when the sun goes down? | *sunset | after | home | walked
exam: Dad says «The phone company is sunsetting our old plan», which means the plan will | *Be shut down | Go on for ever | Be sung about in a song | Be made cheaper for everyone
